    "description": "Tree farm, level 1 of 3: shell and fittings (what soldiers build first). Over budget: 284 blocks vs 102 (the lumber camp brief; the tree farm has no budget of its own), first build 226 vs 200. The lumber camp's tier-6 upgrade: an 11 x 11 fenced plantation (spruce fence on cobblestone corner piers) with three rows of saplings each side of a coarse dirt path, two young oaks from the first planting, and the woodcutter's shed at the back in the sawmill's look (dark oak frame, oak roof with dark oak eaves; chest, grindstone workstation, barrel), a log pile, woodpile, chopping block and composter. L1: plot, gateway posts, shed, empty planting rows (saplings by the decoration step), young trees. L2: saplings in every row (oak, birch, spruce), a lychgate roof with lanterns, lanterns on the piers, a sawhorse, a cauldron and a barrel by the path. L3: a hanging sign (the Studio does not draw hanging signs), banners on the shed, a nursery shelf of potted saplings, bee nests on the oaks, flowers, moss, an axe in the block. Decoration step adds: sapling.",
